## Frontend prompt overlay update

The account editor now shows only a compact prompt input and send button floating over the document. Hover or keyboard focus expands the input; moving away collapses it. The wide assistant background, badge, extra action icons and always-visible help line were removed. Generation errors and proposal review remain accessible. Template selection happens before editing; no template dropdown appears in the editor, and AI proposals cannot switch the selected template.

## Resume library and Home presentation

My Resumes shows each saved resume as the first page of its selected template, with its title underneath; clicking the preview opens the shared editor. Inline view/edit/download actions are removed. PDF downloads remain in the editor; Delete resume is in the editor File menu with confirmation. Legacy non-editable PDFs still open their details page. Thumbnails load owned source only when near the viewport and never record an editor visit. Home places compact curated templates on white above two responsive rows of recently opened resumes on light gray. Catalog selections go directly to the persona/manual choice for that template. No usage analytics were added: trending is a curated catalog section. Recent-opening metadata stores only resume IDs and timestamps in this browser tab's sessionStorage (with an in-memory fallback); it is not a cross-device history or another resume-content store. Only records in the authenticated user's owned list can appear.

Resume HTML preparation retries once after a transient asset-fetch failure, before sending the save request; it does not retry creation requests. A browser regression check deliberately fails the first font fetch to verify recovery.

Gallery update verification: production build, TypeScript and zero-warning ESLint passed. Browser integration passed for actual saved-template thumbnails, direct editor navigation, most-recent-open ordering, different Home backgrounds, compact template initialization, editor deletion and mobile width. The AI editor regression also passed with an intentionally failed first font request to verify preparation retry.

## Shared frontend typography and editor branding

The interface now uses the free template gallery's Arial body text (16px) and Georgia heading family, with shared body, title, section and caption tokens in styles/tokens.css. The same UI hierarchy applies to marketing, authentication, account pages, persona pages, dialogs and galleries. Editor toolbar text stays compact. Resume pages, thumbnails and print/export content retain their template typography and user font choices. The editor header uses the existing resume_logo.png followed by the editable document title on one line; the Resume Builder text and boxed title field are removed. On mobile, the logo/title remain together above the actions.
